ut ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And Phinehas the son of Eleazar was the ruler over them in time past, and the LORD was with him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbAnd Zechariah the son of Meshelemiah was porter of the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÌAll these which were chosen to be porters in the gates were two hundred and twelve. These were reckoned by their genealogy in their villages, whom David and Samuel the seer did ordain in their set office.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚So they and their children had the oversight of the gates of the house of the LORD, namely, the house of the tabernacle, by wards.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKIn four quarters were the porters, toward the east, west, north, and south.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlAnd their brethren, which were in their villages, were to come after seven days from time to time with them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒFor these Levites, the four chief porters, were in their set office, and were over the chambers and treasuries of the house of God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆAnd they lodged round about the house of God, because the charge was upon them, and the opening thereof every morning pertained to them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnAnd certain of them had the charge of the ministering vessels, that they should bring them in and out by tale.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ·Some of them also were appointed to oversee the vessels, and all the instruments of the sanctuary, and the fine flour, and the wine, and the oil, and the frankincense, and the spices.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDAnd some of the sons of the priests made the ointment of the spices.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘And Mattithiah, one of the Levites, who was the firstborn of Shallum the Korahite, had the set office over the things that were made in the pans.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd other of their brethren, of the sons of the Kohathites, were over the shewbread, to prepare it every sabbath.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book§chapter	«first_verse!ªlast_verse"¦verses’„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›And these are the singers, chief of the fathers of the Levites, who remaining in the chambers were free: for they were employed in that work day and night.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeThese chief fathers of the Levites were chief throughout their generations; these dwelt at Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book§chapter	«first_verse#ªlast_verse,¦versesš„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPAnd in Gibeon dwelt the father of Gibeon, Jehiel, whose wife's name was Maachah:¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNand his firstborn son Abdon, then Zur, and Kish, and Baal, and Ner, and Nadab,¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ0and Gedor, and Ahio, and Zechariah, and Mikloth.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAnd Mikloth begat Shimeam. And they also dwelt with their brethren at Jerusalem, over against their brethren.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAnd Ner begat Kish; and Kish begat Saul; and Saul begat Jonathan, and Malchi-shua, and Abinadab, and Eshbaal.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCAnd the son of Jonathan was Merib-baal: and Merib-baal begat Micah.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEAnd the sons of Micah were, Pithon, and Melech, and Tahrea, and Ahaz.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]And Ahaz begat Jarah; and Jarah begat Alemeth, and Azmaveth, and Zimri; and Zimri begat Moza;¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJand Moza begat Binea; and Rephaiah his son, Eleasah his son, Azel his son.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd Azel had six sons, whose names are these, Azrikam, Bocheru, and Ishmael, and Sheariah, and Obadiah, and Hanan: these were the sons of Azel.¦layout ªlast_verse,